Emerging Opportunities
Solid-State and Silicon-Anode Batteries
Next-generation battery designs offer potential improvements in energy storage, device size, and performance. Commercial opportunities will depend on manufacturing scalability, cost competitiveness, reliability, and successful integration into consumer products.

Wireless Charging Compatibility
As wireless charging becomes more common across consumer devices, battery and device manufacturers have opportunities to improve charging efficiency, heat management, and compatibility across product ecosystems.

Battery Recycling and Circular Supply Chains
Growing attention to material recovery and resource efficiency is creating opportunities for battery recycling technologies, recovered-material processing, and improved end-of-life collection systems. These solutions can help reduce waste while supporting access to critical battery materials.

Companies that combine manufacturing efficiency with dependable performance, cost management, and investment in advanced chemistries may be well positioned to respond to evolving consumer electronics requirements.

